1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,260
One dream.

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:04,660
One wish.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:08,240
If you want it, gotta go over the top.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

5
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,380
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

7
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,877
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

8
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:41,417
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

9
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,160
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

10
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,417
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

11
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,440
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

12
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,557
Despite all that to run is not an option.

13
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,637
Once they're closed, I
feel the satisfaction.

14
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

15
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,020
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

16
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,317
If you are going on your way.

17
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,737
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

19
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,217
Yes, I can.

20
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,057
As you're on your way.

21
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,357
Marks maps will be made.

22
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:27,197
Yes, with every step that you will take.

23
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

24
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead at new horizons.

25
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,977
In view shining brightly.

26
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,880
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you.

27
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,117
Dream living, that's the way.

28
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,197
Make like a hurricane.

29
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:45,100
Now, got to make your mark today.

30
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,997
One dream, one wish.

31
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

32
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,917
Go for the knockout.

33
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,980
Over the top!

34
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,360
Kawamatsu!

35
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,480
My dear friend!

36
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,160
I'd lost hope!

37
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:20,580
Yet here you are before me!

38
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,230
Indeed.

39
00:02:23,313 --> 00:02:26,607
And all it took was 13 years of
poisonous fish, day after day.

40
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:31,400
Let me see your face, Kawamatsu.

41
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,580
Alas, I am bound by chains.

42
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,860
When will the battle occur?

43
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:44,396
Nine days from now, on the
night of the fire festival.

44
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:49,297
Ah, what delicious irony, taking Kaido's
head in the celebration meant to honor him.

45
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:53,820
I'm sorry to ask this, but could
you please free me from here?

46
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,020
Of course I will.

47
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:59,180
I'll see to it post-haste, though
I'm faced with several obstacles.

48
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:02,357
I'll need the keys to
your cell and your chains.

49
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,040
Let us hope they aren't
too rusted to open.

50
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:06,570
Hold on.

51
00:03:06,653 --> 00:03:08,517
There's someone in front
of the forbidden cell.

52
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,776
His head is massive.

53
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:11,377
That's got to be the key thief.

54
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,540
We found the guy.

55
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,294
Commander Solitaire, what should we do?

56
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,350
Un-key!

57
00:03:17,433 --> 00:03:18,720
Capture him, you fools!

58
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,620
Uh-oh.

59
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,040
Smoke escaped Jutsu!

60
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,280
He disappeared!

61
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,940
Must be a ninja! Find him!

62
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,680
Oh, right.

63
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:39,017
I think we have enough guards going
after the key thief right now.

64
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:40,360
Let's party!

65
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:51,750
Good.

66
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:56,120
Now escort these gentlemen
to their execution. Yes, sir!

67
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,880
Come on, this way.

68
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:01,520
Here we go, baby!

69
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:03,110
Yeah!

70
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:26,500
It's Master Queen's special device
performance, the Sumo Inferno!

71
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,310
Sumo?

72
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,210
What the hell?

73
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:40,080
This collar here is the same as
the ones you got around your necks.

74
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,940
Imagine this stone pillar is one of you.

75
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:47,257
Now let's see what happens if you try
to leave the ring with your collar on,

76
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:48,170
shall we?

77
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:55,480
Whoa, that's intense.

78
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:58,120
So before trying anything naughty,

79
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:00,457
you should know that these
collars are equipped with blades.

80
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:02,599
strong enough to cut through stone.

81
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:07,860
Or in this case, your
little necks. No fair!

82
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,691
It's like what the Celestial Dragons used!

83
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,277
I appreciate the spirit,

84
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:15,357
kid, but you really think you can
pull the thing off just like that?

85
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:20,060
Keep winning matches, and your head
gets to stay attached to your neck.

86
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,980
But step out of the
ring and you're a toast.

87
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:24,797
You two are a team, by the way,

88
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:28,137
so the execution isn't complete until
both of you fall out of the ring.

89
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:30,917
Also, if you change your
mind and decide to join us,

90
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,440
then Straw Hat and only
Straw Hat will be released.

91
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:39,900
As for your opponents, they'll have
weapons, no collars, and limitless numbers.

92
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:42,980
I'll keep them coming
for as long as I choose.

93
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:46,534
So I'll do you one favor,
just to make things more fair.

94
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:50,076
Let's uncuff you, boys, so
you don't die in round one.

95
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,760
Huh? What?

96
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,376
After all the trouble I went through?

97
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:00,440
Was this the wrong key?

98
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:03,386
So the mission was a
bust from the very start?

99
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:06,100
Thank you!

100
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,757
I thought you were a bad guy,
but you're actually pretty nice.

101
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:13,037
With those dumb cuffs off,
I'm practically free already.

102
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:13,950
What?

103
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:15,437
But I just put something
even worse on you.

104
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:19,461
Did you forget you're wearing a
collar that can chop your head off?

105
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:20,530
What?

106
00:06:20,613 --> 00:06:21,443
Oh, that's right.

107
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:22,820
Wait a minute.

108
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:26,537
If the two of us have to fight as
a team, then I'll only hold Mr.

109
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:27,502
Straw Hat back.

110
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,522
Can't you execute us separately?

111
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,620
Hey, Balloon!

112
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,460
Oh, Balloon!

113
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,700
Please don't provoke him.

114
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:41,880
If I kick your round ass hard enough,
will you let us out of this place?

115
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,280
There you are.

116
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,620
So you're the bastard
who stole my sword, huh?

117
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,520
I'll be taking it back now.

118
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:13,180
You are the one who
stole that sacred blade.

119
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:21,880
I have reclaimed Shusui and returned
it to the only place that it belongs.

120
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,977
That flamed sword is a
national treasure that

121
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:28,420
was taken from the grave of
the legendary samurai, Ryuma.

122
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:30,780
Yeah, I know.

123
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:34,220
Then shut your mouth and leave this place.

124
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:42,440
If you do not, I will gladly steal
the two swords at your waist as well.

125
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,560
I warn you.

126
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,580
You a weapon collector or what?

127
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,720
That's quite a haul.

128
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:51,359
What are you going to do with them?

129
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:56,877
As it turns out, my friends could put
those weapons to good use right now.

130
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:58,700
Lucky timing, you might say.

131
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,260
Since you think stealing is fair game.

132
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,180
I'll take everything you've got!

133
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:18,440
You should have fled while you
had the chance, mountain bandit!

134
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:24,364
Sorry, but there seems
to be a misunderstanding.

135
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:28,200
To be clear, I'm a pirate.

136
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:50,680
Oh, I'm going to enjoy crushing you.

137
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,420
He'll learn soon.

138
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,169
A couple of rounds and
he'll beg for mercy.

139
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:06,880
The rules are completely stacked against
him, and he's too stupid to see it.

140
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:10,156
He thinks this is a tournament
when it's an execution.

141
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:15,040
All right, men, start lining up.

142
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,474
You all get your shot.

143
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:17,720
Show them hell!

144
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:27,202
Deathmatch, go!

145
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:30,300
No, there's too many of them.

146
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:34,717
Not only do we outnumber you,
we're all armed to the teeth.

147
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,800
We don't have to follow any rules.

148
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,140
Is it starting to sink in?

149
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:43,657
It's only a matter of time before
both of you are chopped to bits.

150
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:53,269
Yes, let's go!

151
00:09:53,352 --> 00:09:54,182
Rest in peace, old man, yo.

152
00:09:54,265 --> 00:09:56,040
Rest in peace, Mr. Straw Hat.

153
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,720
Positions ready!

154
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,000
Get ready!

155
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:04,290
Go!

156
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:09,657
You prisoners are lucky to get
a front row seat to the murder

157
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:14,980
show better behave or it'll be
you up here next Ha ha ha ha!

158
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,060
Keep them coming!

159
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:39,026
Those guys weren't even
a good enough warm-up!

160
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,977
Are you kidding me?

161
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:46,589
He didn't even touch them!

162
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,390
Oh.

163
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:54,480
So he can use the Conqueror's Haki.

164
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,760
Who are you?

165
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:06,457
All right, it's time to up the ante.

166
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,760
Pleasures!

167
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,300
It's your time to shine!

168
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:20,680
It's been an uproar every
day since you showed up.

169
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:27,480
But if you can protect Yoguro,
that's all that matters.

170
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:34,960
I'm counting on you, Lufitaro.

171
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:42,180
It's a raid.

172
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,577
That's Hawkins.

173
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:52,157
He's a headliner from the Beast Pirates.

174
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,300
No one moves an inch.

175
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,837
This is a bathhouse.

176
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,880
What could you want from us?

177
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:02,797
A bathhouse is perfect for
our job today If everyone's

178
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:05,821
naked that means they can't
hide anything from us.

179
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,220
Hey, Drake, get in here.

180
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,518
What are you doing?

181
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:12,437
There's nothing of interest
to me in the bathhouse.

182
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,461
My job is to take down Sabo Mask.

183
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:18,401
You can do the rest of the
dirty work on your own.

184
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,885
What are we gonna do, Shinobu?

185
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:25,117
If they sent in someone like Hawkins,
then they must be here for us.

186
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,157
How did they know where to find us?

187
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:30,317
Those cheaters, literally
catching us with our pants down.

188
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:31,282
Shall we fight?

189
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,720
We'll keep that as a last resort.

190
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,180
A mature woman doesn't use
her weapons carelessly.

191
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,840
Hide behind me, ladies, quickly.

192
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:47,180
Now, I want everyone here to line up.

193
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,576
Show us your ankles.

194
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:52,097
If any of you have a reversed
crescent moon tattoo,

195
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:54,768
then I'm afraid you'll
need to come with me.

196
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:01,175
Everyone soaking in the bath
must step out immediately.

197
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,420
They know about that?

198
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:05,169
How is that even possible?

199
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,640
Check them all. Yes!

200
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:09,760
Did the plan get leaked?

201
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:22,340
Who is that hiding behind you?

202
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,100
Show yourself!

203
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:32,520
Don't worry, I'll back you
up if something happens.

204
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:38,220
Oh, sorry, did you mean
me? I wasn't hiding.

205
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:41,127
I'm just a normal customer
taking a hot bath.

206
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,260
So it's you.

207
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,860
She's dynamite!

208
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:00,924
Her body's a national treasure!

209
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,280
A deadly art.

210
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:06,720
Come on, seriously?

211
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:11,160
A happy punch straight to my heart!

212
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:13,700
Bandits, a knockout!

213
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:15,550
What?

214
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:21,400
Wait, that's the guy from yesterday.

215
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:22,840
Soap mask!

216
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,300
Nami.

217
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:31,940
The shape of your body was like a
magnificent river flowing through heaven.

218
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:36,540
Sanchi, what is he doing here?

219
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:38,720
And what is he wearing, that idiot?

220
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:41,780
Hey, Drake, is silver mask inside?

221
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:43,333
He was there all along.

222
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:46,980
Hey, bring me silver mask!

223
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,590
Huh?

224
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:51,420
I said...

225
00:14:56,020 --> 00:15:00,397
If you're that weak to naked women, then
you should have informed me beforehand.

226
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,240
Who you calling weak?

227
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:09,000
Drake, you're originally from
the North Blue, aren't you?

228
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:11,700
Yeah, same as you. What of it?

229
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:16,160
Then look, that man should seem familiar.

230
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:24,050
Ugh!

231
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,157
Stealth black from Germa double six!

232
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,580
But Al, why?

233
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,540
Don't you dare run from us!

234
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:37,560
The search isn't over yet!

235
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,019
Come on, let's go!

236
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:41,180
You filler!

237
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,127
You think I'm afraid of you?

238
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:46,200
Look out, Sabo Mask!

239
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,720
It seems he has
teleportation tech as well.

240
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,060
Hang on tight, ladies.

241
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,740
He's flying! Follow him!

242
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:04,417
Only Stealth Black could
have pulled that off.

243
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,200
I'll get him next time.

244
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:10,008
You wanna explain yourself?

245
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,540
It's a long story.

246
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,445
I'll tell you once we're safe.

247
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:16,640
You're bleeding. Profusely.

248
00:16:17,020 --> 00:16:20,280
If I die now, I die happy. I'll be fine.

249
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:25,657
That's the least of our concerns now that
they've found out about the ankle tattoos.

250
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:26,570
Indeed.

251
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:29,780
It seems we have a traitor
in our midst. Yeah.

252
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,757
And I'm afraid that's not all.

253
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:34,837
I heard some more bad news
before I went to the bathhouse.

254
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:37,626
Beppo, Penguin, and
Chouchou were taken captive.

255
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:40,968
The Beast Pirates must
be aiming for Traffy.

256
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:44,157
They nabbed his friends to
use his bait to lure him out.

257
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:46,577
In that case, it's likely
their plan will work.

258
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:49,425
He may be a grump, but
he cares about his crew.

259
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:53,297
We'll try to stop him for now.

260
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:56,204
We can't afford to throw
the capital into chaos.

261
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:00,054
You still haven't told us why
you were at the bathhouse.

262
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:13,060
How much longer till I get my yummy treat?

263
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:16,280
I'm gonna pass out soon if I don't eat.

264
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,520
Are we there yet?

265
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:22,680
Tell me, Chuck Raymond, I
would love a little snack.

266
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:25,100
You're giving me that look again!

267
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:28,520
It shouldn't be too much longer, Olene!

268
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:29,620
Hang in there!

269
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,360
First, we say big bow!

270
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,197
After that...

271
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:38,120
It's time to Shit!

272
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,780
I'm something big!

273
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,110
Yes!

274
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:46,597
Will you also enjoy a bowl with me, Otama?

275
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:47,510
Huh?

276
00:17:47,593 --> 00:17:48,740
Yes, ma 'am.

277
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:50,380
It's the best.

278
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,779
Otsuru gave me some on my birthday.

279
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:54,337
I'll never forget it.

280
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:56,832
It's like it was dancing inside my mouth.

281
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:01,077
It's a happiness spread all the way
from my head down to my tippy toes.

282
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:03,278
I thought my ginger bubble exploded.

283
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:05,020
It was so yummy.

284
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,280
Yep, that's right.

285
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,100
Red beans are such a delight.

286
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:14,340
Red bean paste, don't let
it go to waste. Ah-ha.

287
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:15,710
Rice cake.

288
00:18:15,793 --> 00:18:17,760
Best friends with red beans!

289
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:21,180
Together they make the
most deliciousest treat!

290
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:24,020
I bet that you can't name a Tsuru bear!

291
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:25,950
Agreed!

292
00:18:26,033 --> 00:18:31,320
And the way the little pieces of mochi
shine like a frog's eye, it's collectible!

293
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,240
Sorry, like a what?

294
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:37,740
Wait a sec.

295
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:40,175
You don't eat eyeballs, do you, Olene?

296
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:41,930
No!

297
00:18:42,013 --> 00:18:43,894
I was just pointing out the similarity.

298
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:48,400
Though almost anything
looks good, my dear.

299
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:51,600
I'm not edible! Stop! Mama!

300
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:55,500
If I can't get it, I'll go mad.

301
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:57,837
You're rather excited over this meal.

302
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,391
Your certainness is okay?

303
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,380
They don't know anymore. Huh?

304
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:04,300
I must stop!

305
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:09,749
What's gonna happen when she
finds out there is no Oshiruko?

306
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:13,677
Is the devastating truth gonna
shock her back into being big mom?

307
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:15,140
STRIKE!

308
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:22,548
This is going to make the rescue
mission even more dangerous!

309
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:25,820
What should I do?

310
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,400
What can I do?

311
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:28,740
Oh, man!

312
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,517
Another survey!

313
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:42,720
Right away!

314
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,720
Luffy Toto wins!

315
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:25,320
He did it!

316
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:27,120
That's amazing.

317
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,911
You took down all the pleasures with ease.

318
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:35,830
Almost.

319
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,711
What do you mean, almost?

320
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,697
You wiped the floor with those guys.

321
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,060
I don't get how Rayleigh does it.

322
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:44,100
I think, like this, maybe?

323
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,320
Rayleigh? Yeah.

324
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:52,340
Luffy, it's called armament Haki.

325
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:56,019
Think of it as covering
yourself in invisible armor.

326
00:20:57,120 --> 00:21:01,360
I watched Rayleigh send an elephant
flying without even touching it.

327
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:07,051
That's the first time he showed me Haki.

328
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:09,600
It must have been insanely strong.

329
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:12,220
I need to learn how to use that.

330
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:14,460
This is taking too long!

331
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:19,445
Just let me get in there already, I'll
kill that little punk in ten seconds flat!

332
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:24,440
What would be the fun in that, huh?

333
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:28,100
Sumo Inferno's at its best
when it's dragged out. Huh?

334
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:31,140
Look, I'll break it down for you.

335
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:34,337
The more people involved,
the longer the fight.

336
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:36,357
The longer the fight,
the more the suffering.

337
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:38,997
This whole production
is about crushing his

338
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:42,697
spirit slowly but surely until he croaks.

339
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:45,957
Get out of here with that efficiency crap!

340
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:48,337
This is about entertainment.

341
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:52,137
Which you clearly don't
know the first thing about?

342
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:54,280
Why don't you go and fetch me more?

343
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:55,710
Another?

344
00:21:55,820 --> 00:21:57,437
Damn, haven't you had enough?

345
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,240
Slow it down Go to hell!

346
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:00,717
It's more than just food.

347
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,457
It's like air to me.

348
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:03,537
For you, sir.

349
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:04,777
Uh-huh!

350
00:22:04,860 --> 00:22:08,380
Ah, what impeccable time
is exactly what I wanted.

351
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,017
This is my all-time favorite.

352
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,040
How'd you know?

353
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,840
It's Supreee-me.

354
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:21,000
Send him flying with my invisible armor.

355
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,960
I'll figure it out somehow.

356
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:25,110
Mr.

357
00:22:25,193 --> 00:22:27,540
Straw Hat, what are you talking about?

358
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,270
All right.

359
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:31,120
Let's practice.

360
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,718
Give me your worst.

361
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,760
I actually met with Yuma, you know.

362
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:45,460
How dare you lie!

363
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:55,400
What do you claim is impossible?

364
00:22:57,120 --> 00:23:00,577
Did you think I would fall
for such an obvious ruse?

365
00:23:00,660 --> 00:23:05,077
I mean, I saw his body, the
soul was someone else's.

366
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:07,520
Sounds like you've lost your mind to me!

367
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:11,040
You know nothing of Ryuma!

368
00:23:11,860 --> 00:23:13,660
He was a legendary swordsman,

369
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:17,620
able to take down any opponents
in the blink of an eye!

370
00:23:19,740 --> 00:23:24,680
You're an ingrate, incapable of
understanding the greatness of Shusui!

371
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:32,320
That blade is a treasure to the
people here, IT BELONGS TO REYUMON!

372
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:41,277
Many years ago, the world once
referred to our beloved country.

373
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:44,220
as the Land of Gold. Oh yeah?

374
00:23:44,700 --> 00:23:46,140
Then why is that?

375
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:47,490
You're open!

376
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:55,800
Pirates across the world lusted
after the wealth of our land.

377
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,997
And the world nobles too.

378
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:00,460
They longed to rule over us.

379
00:24:02,320 --> 00:24:07,740
However, there was only one man who stood
up to the avaricious enemies from abroad.

380
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:13,060
He burned the name of our samurai
into the pages of history.

381
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:18,280
That man was our hero, Ryuma.

382
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:23,780
Many legends surround his name.

383
00:24:24,660 --> 00:24:27,940
However, one in particular
is the most famous.

384
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:33,580
It's a tale of him slaying a dragon
that once flew over the capital.

385
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:39,000
Upon his death, he was laid to rest
with his trusted weapon, Chouchou.

386
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:42,020
He was consecrated as God of the Blade!

387
00:24:42,820 --> 00:24:45,940
Ryuma and Chouchou belong
to the people of Wano!

388
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:58,620
Fine, then.

389
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:00,780
You made your point.

390
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:08,940
But you know, none of that's
got anything to do with me.

391
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:13,180
It's time for me to take back Shusui.

392
00:25:13,540 --> 00:25:16,540
I feel off my game
swinging around two swords.

393
00:25:18,620 --> 00:25:21,740
It seems as if I have overestimated you.

394
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:30,160
Shusui is a black blade It is Ryumas You
are not the one who forged it in battle

395
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:34,277
You're not a swordsman like he was You're

396
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:37,600
just a hoodlum With no
integrity to speak of

397
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,230
Forged?

398
00:25:39,480 --> 00:25:41,600
I was wondering about that

399
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,720
Someone help!

400
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:50,910
Huh?

401
00:25:50,993 --> 00:25:52,060
You're open!

402
00:25:54,820 --> 00:25:56,100
You asshole!

403
00:25:57,660 --> 00:26:00,817
Don't stab me in the back when
someone is crying for help!

404
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:03,717
You thought I wouldn't take
advantage of an opening?

405
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:06,200
This is a fight to the death I will win!

406
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,420
Please save us!

407
00:26:11,620 --> 00:26:14,340
Our lives are in danger! Look!

408
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:15,720
It's a samurai!

409
00:26:17,140 --> 00:26:17,970
Hey!

410
00:26:18,053 --> 00:26:19,380
Can you help us?

411
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:21,840
Are they serious?

412
00:26:22,180 --> 00:26:24,080
The laughing is throwing me off.

413
00:26:25,940 --> 00:26:26,770
Mr.

414
00:26:26,853 --> 00:26:27,683
Swordsman, sir!

415
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:28,740
I beg of you!

416
00:26:28,940 --> 00:26:29,822
Please help us!

417
00:26:31,820 --> 00:26:32,650
Blood.

418
00:26:32,733 --> 00:26:34,420
Guess they're serious after all.

419
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:05,740
One second, wait!

420
00:27:06,120 --> 00:27:07,480
You're open!

421
00:27:14,220 --> 00:27:16,240
I told you to wait!

422
00:27:20,520 --> 00:27:21,350
Damn it!

423
00:27:21,433 --> 00:27:22,988
Can't you take a hint, man?

424
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,760
We are still in a duel!

425
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,660
I am not finished with you yet! I know!

426
00:27:27,900 --> 00:27:29,900
We'll fight, but give me a minute!

427
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:46,320
You think everyone forgot about
the murder you committed, Zorojuro?

428
00:27:58,520 --> 00:28:02,580
Here's a question, what
compels you to help them?

429
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:05,777
What about you?

430
00:28:05,860 --> 00:28:07,677
Why do you have a beef with them?

431
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:09,337
I'm here for one thing,

432
00:28:09,420 --> 00:28:13,420
to cut down that little brat who
laughed at the shogun and ran away!

433
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:19,980
It's all right, Dock. I'm here.

434
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:23,360
I know who you are.

435
00:28:24,500 --> 00:28:27,800
Yojito Kirikamazo, the serial
killer from the capital.

436
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:31,797
But it's clear you're actually an
assassin that works for Orochi.

437
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:35,917
Who else would have reason to come after
a harmless young girl's life like this?

438
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:39,900
The nerve of you addressing the
Shogun without his proper title.

439
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:41,677
You're an interesting one.

440
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:43,380
Who are you?

441
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:46,506
You're a samurai, aren't you?

442
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:47,780
Please help us.

443
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:51,160
Well, lucky for you,

444
00:28:51,300 --> 00:28:53,117
I'm not exactly the type of man to watch a

445
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:55,965
woman and a kid get
slaughtered before my eyes.

446
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:58,620
I'll do anything to pay you back.

447
00:28:59,460 --> 00:29:01,800
We'll call it even for a meal and sake.

448
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:03,670
Deal.

449
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:08,040
Well, I'm in.

450
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:20,520
Fine by me, I was already granted permission
to dismantle anyone who gets in my way.

451
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:26,717
I'm sure I'm gonna catch hell from your
boss, but I'm kicking your ass either way.

452
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:32,077
Not to worry—you'll be dead before
you can even catch your breath!

453
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:32,990
breath

454
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:16,460
He's pretty tough.

455
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:03,240
It's about time you got serious.

456
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,717
You're lucky I don't have my sword.

457
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:42,160
This would be easy.

458
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:56,660
I'm unbearably hungry.

459
00:31:56,980 --> 00:32:00,000
Do you think that maybe,
if I'm all a meal good,

460
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:03,024
I could get dibs on a
stash of prison dumplings?

461
00:32:05,540 --> 00:32:06,500
That's fine.

462
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:07,976
Show him who's boss.

463
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,997
That's what I like to hear.

464
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:11,780
Thanks for the positivity.

465
00:32:12,280 --> 00:32:14,400
I'm going to get him. You what?

466
00:32:14,660 --> 00:32:16,320
Now prepare yourself!

467
00:32:29,700 --> 00:32:30,980
Nice try.

468
00:32:31,820 --> 00:32:33,560
But that barely hurts.

469
00:32:36,220 --> 00:32:37,320
Please, Mr.

470
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:38,457
Straw Hat, just wait.

471
00:32:38,540 --> 00:32:41,540
I know he looks quite
cuddly on the exterior.

472
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:44,517
But keep in mind the bear's
claws are powerful enough?

473
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:46,917
to tear through human
flesh like it's paper.

474
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,100
Be on your guard.

475
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,740
I'll send you fly!

476
00:32:57,460 --> 00:32:58,600
No contact!

477
00:33:15,060 --> 00:33:15,890
Sucks!

478
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:19,620
Keep accidentally hitting them!

479
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:21,257
Wait, what do you mean?

480
00:33:21,340 --> 00:33:23,399
Isn't hitting them the whole point?

481
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:25,360
What are you trying to do?

482
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:27,657
It's fine.

483
00:33:27,740 --> 00:33:29,100
Send in more!

484
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:30,520
Come on!

485
00:33:38,540 --> 00:33:39,370
Ah!

486
00:33:47,600 --> 00:33:48,430
Shit!

487
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:52,760
Ha! Ha! Ha!

488
00:34:22,500 --> 00:34:23,700
Oh, Brad!

489
00:34:36,740 --> 00:34:38,100
Oh, Brad!

490
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:56,800
I can't pull it out!

491
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:10,285
Hope you don't mind if
I borrow this for a sec.

492
00:35:23,300 --> 00:35:24,557
What is he doing?

493
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:28,080
He's trying to use three weapons?

494
00:35:32,380 --> 00:35:34,960
Three-sword style!

495
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:39,880
Purgatory!

496
00:35:48,940 --> 00:35:49,770
Onigiri!

497
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,760
Ah!

498
00:36:26,140 --> 00:36:28,120
What strength! Stunning!

499
00:36:37,480 --> 00:36:39,160
And here he comes.

500
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:41,300
I really have to do this now?

501
00:37:17,480 --> 00:37:18,960
Mr. Samurai!

502
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:25,470
Thank you.
